==Swedish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gml|sv}} {{term|kort|lang=gml}}, an early borrowing from {{etyl|la|sv}} {{term|curtus|lang=la}}.<ref name=seb/> Cognate with German {{term|kurz|lang=de}}, Dutch {{term|kort|lang=nl}}, Danish {{term|kort|lang=da}} and Norwegian {{term|kort|lang=no}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/kɔrt/|lang=sv}}
* {{audio|Sv-kort.ogg|audio|lang=sv}}

====Adjective====
{{sv-adj}}

# [[short]]
#* '''1901''', {{w|Zacharias Topelius}}, [http://runeberg.org/topnovel/b0313.html ''Noveller'']
#*: Thomas! Thomas! [...]viskade nu Lotten, ty det var den '''korte''' som segrat, och hon hade igenkänt honom.
#*:: Thomas! Thomas! Lotten now whispered, since it was the short one that had won, and she had recognized him.
#* '''1931''', {{w|Hjalmar Bergman}}, [http://runeberg.org/clownjac/05.html ''Clownen Jac'']
#*: '''Kortaste''' avståndet mellan två punkter är den krokiga linjen, ju krokigare, desto '''kortare'''.
#*:: The shortest distance between two points is the crooked line, the more crooked, the shorter.

=====Declension=====
{{sv-adj-reg|n=kort}}

=====Antonyms=====
* [[lång]]

=====Derived terms=====
* [[korthet]]
* [[kortbyxor]]

===Etymology 2===
Probably from {{etyl|da|sv}} {{term|kort||a card|lang=da}} or possibly from a not referenced {{etyl|gml|sv}} word {{term|kort|lang=gml}} known in Low German, {{term|kort||a card|lang=nds}}.<ref name=seb>[http://runeberg.org/svetym/0434.html ''Svensk etymologisk ordbok'' ("Swedish etymological dictionary", in Swedish)]</ref> Cognate with Icelandic {{term|kort||a card, a map|lang=is}} and Faroese {{term|kort||a card, a map|lang=fo}}, both from {{etyl|non|sv}} {{term|kort||a map|lang=non}}, a variant of the Latin words {{term|charta|lang=la}} and {{term|carta|lang=la}}.<ref name=seb/>

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/kʊrt/|lang=sv}}

====Noun====
{{sv-noun|n}}

# a [[card]]; a piece of stiff paper or plastic.
#* '''1926''', John Wahlborg, [http://runeberg.org/sistresa/18.html ''Sista resan'']
#*: Mannen räckte mig ett litet '''kort''', varpå han nedskrivit namn och adress på en kvinna i Stockholm.
#*:: The man gave me a small card on which he had written the name and address of a woman in Stockholm.
# a [[playing card]]
# a [[card game]], a game involving playing cards
#: ''Ska vi spela '''kort'''?''
#:: Shall we play cards?
# [[photograph]]

=====Declension=====
{{sv-noun-n-zero}}

